Pywel Atlas combined v0.111 map markers (v0.111: route line on the world map's own canvas, called after each world-map update; v0.110: completion tracker: per-region collected counts for the filter panel and the always-on widget (game regions, region-map.h), widget place and options in filters.ini; v0.109: chest card stat lines restyled like the inventory tooltip (style 3: two-column stat rows with stat icons, effect lines in the buff style with their own game icon, needs UI add-on v0.80), no blank lines; Vigor effect fixed (buff levels matched by number); v0.108: unique gear markers (chest icon type 226, 43 one-of-a-kind items, hidden once collected: reward items when their reward stage is completed, ground and quest items when picked up); v0.107: route line drawn with small stop dots and hidden on the world map while a knowledge card is open (route files only); Abyss Cresset hover text is just "Abyss Cresset"; v0.106: chest and Abyss chest knowledge cards list the item base stats (Attack, Defense, stat levels, gear effects) in the inventory tooltip font, siphon gear with a one-line explanation; v0.105: Abyss Cresset markers (game icon type 340, 101 cressets, hidden once their challenge mission is completed; F8 catalogue also lists the StandStone icons); v0.104: route line support: route stops (spots shown and not done, unknown or quest-locked) and read-only world-map and minimap view copies for the route overlay; v0.103: chest and Abyss chest card icons get a size class (pywel-icon-60..90, drawn by the UI add-on v0.79) so they look about the same size; v0.102: Abyss chest labels name their item; Abyss chests open the knowledge card (item, description, also-contains, item icon); v0.101: Abyss chests behind a quest stay hidden until it is done (quest pass over QuestSaveData); chest card picture via the name-copy hook 0x3d5f80, since 0x388e00 differed in memory; v0.100: chest knowledge cards show the item's inventory icon (stringinfo row swap at the card's picture lookup, name-checked); v0.99: Hernand strongbox 1 (sliding jigsaw) is an empty decoy: no marker, not counted; v0.98: our knowledge cards get their whole description as markup, one line per part with real line breaks (artifact steps and reward, recipe lines); v0.97: Abyss-island Nexus markers use the surface Nexus icon (type 234; type 235 followed the map camera); v0.96: knowledge card markup observation, logs only (format-text 0x647cb0, set-markup 0x3ed7f90 inside the card layout); v0.95: Abyss-island Nexus markers (type 235, 51 on the Abyss map, hidden once activated; the 2 Nexuses at Kliff's houses join the surface Nexuses, now 215); v0.94: lines inside a card paragraph joined with a middle dot (the card shows no line breaks); v0.93: Sealed Abyss Artifact markers open a knowledge card (challenge name, steps, reward); v0.92: chest card description as two paragraphs (item type, item text), no markup, generic chest paragraph blanked; v0.91: chest markers with a known item open the map's knowledge card (Treasure Chest card, item name as title, type and item description); v0.90: Sealed Abyss Artifact save read fixed (it rejected saves with two field containers, so every artifact was unknown); v0.89: knowledge card observation, logs only: focus fields, card fill, knowledge key, card layout texts; v0.88: Sealed Abyss Artifact markers (type 187, 141 artifacts, hidden once picked up; tooltip with the artifact's name); v0.87: chest contents on a second map-label line through <br>; v0.86: map tooltip texts on one line; Bells and Nexuses show their name only; v0.85: map tooltips for our markers (chest contents, Bell/shrine names, Nexus) through the game's own map label; v0.84: map tooltip observation, phase 0: logs tooltip text requests and map focus changes, no visible change; v0.83: Abyss Nexus markers turned off in the panel or with F10 are hidden with the game's own hide-reason function (bit 23) instead of removed, and shown again when turned on; read-only observation: layer settings of our icon types, hide bits of our world-map markers right after creation, Abyss Nexus hide-bit changes by name, 4 watched Nexus, 2 chest and 2 Abyss chest markers per round at 3 s / 10 s and on layer changes, with picture objects, container-list check and raw copies; markers on the world map and the minimap; surface Abyss Nexus markers (game icon type 234) until activated; minimap markers created with their own number and adopted once the game has built them; Greymane Shrine markers on, world map needs the Shrine Icons file mod; F8 lists icon types with a world-map look; game type 186/40/41 creations logged, our own markers left out of the sample list) - one native Bell icon (type 360) per not-completed Bell, one chest icon (type 226) per not-opened chest of the game's dedicated chest levels, caves/dungeons, puzzle strongboxes and house chests (190 chests; strongboxes from the save's field-object list, unknown ones hidden) and one chest icon (type 226) per not-opened Abyss chest (74, Abyss map layer) in the detected save, shown at every map zoom (zoom limit off on our own markers only); Greymane Shrine markers on (game shrine icon, type 186); up to 256 markers per category, checked 32 per map update; F10 hides all, F6 shows again. A failed marker is retried every 5 s without blocking others. Observation: zoom windows per icon type, map zoom on F8, player position from the minimap, world-create records (ours and the game's own shrine/Bell icons)
